{"arrivo":"de","origine":"he","origine_nome":"Hebrew","n":44,"parole":[{"parola":"-i","pos":"suffix","n_etimologia":2,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"an unproductive ending of nouns for Semitic and Indo-Iranian groups, especially peoples","termine_origine":"־י","catena":[{"codice":"he","nome":"Hebrew","termine":"־י","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ar","nome":"Arabic","termine":"ي","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"fa","nome":"Persian","termine":"ـی","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"hi","nome":"Hindi","termine":"-ई","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"hi","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From various sources, chiefly Hebrew ־י (-ī), Arabic ي (-iyy), Persian ـی (-ī), and Hindi -ई (-ī)."},{"parola":"abnippeln","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Uncertain; Possibly; perhaps; alternatively","significato":"to die, to kick the bucket","termine_origine":"נבל","catena":[{"codice":"he","nome":"Hebrew","termine":"נבל","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"he","ambiti":[],"via":"yi","testo":"From earlier abnibbeln, originally chiefly in Berlin. Further origin uncertain. Duden suggests ab- (“off”) + nibbeln (“to nibble”), perhaps from a sense of being nibbled away to nothing. Alternatively, possibly from Rotwelsch, by way of Yiddish, ultimately derived from Hebrew נבל (navál, “to wither,"},{"parola":"Behemoth","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"behemoth","termine_origine":"בְּהֵמוֹת","catena":[{"codice":"he","nome":"Hebrew","termine":"בְּהֵמוֹת","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"he","ambiti":["religione"],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Hebrew בְּהֵמוֹת (behemót)."},{"parola":"Bluträcher","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"calco","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Probably","significato":"blood avenger; avenger of blood (one who takes revenge on behalf of a killed person, as in a blood feud)","termine_origine":"גֹּאֵל